        {
            "number": 2,
            "revision": "847b0d518cc7e42dea6674e155baff06b8d560de",
            "parents": [
                "1fb6478f73ef9af0a0a3c8a134c0d53335efaff3"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/28/90428/2",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Ryan-CJ-Huang",
                "email": "ryan_huang@jabil.com",
                "username": "Ryan-CJ-Huang"
            },
            "createdOn": 1779332417,
            "author": {
                "name": "Ryan-CJ-Huang",
                "email": "ryan_huang@jabil.com",
                "username": "Ryan-CJ-Huang"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Konstantin Aladyshev",
                        "email": "aladyshev22@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Kostr"
                    },
                    "message": "To share some personal experience I think I've encountered several RDE devices that return data beyond the main root SFLV value length.\n\nI had problems with several SmartNIC cards with Intel E810 chips on \"Settings\" resources (`Settings`, `Ports/<x>/<y>/Settings` , `NetworkDeviceFunctions/<x>/Settings`...)\n\nFor example here is the answer from GET for the `Settings` resource:\n```\nBEJ Set\n  BEJ String (@odata.etag = W/\\\"77880D60\\\")\n  BEJ Resource Link (@odata.id = %L11)\n  BEJ String (@odata.type = #NetworkAdapter.v1_9_0.NetworkAdapter)\n  BEJ String (Id = Settings)\n  BEJ Boolean (LLDPEnabled = True)\n  BEJ String (Name = E810 Network Adapter Current Setting)\nBEJ Enum <------------------------------ ???\n```\n\nThe last enum has the following values:\n```\n// bejTupleS\n0x01\n0x04 // Major schema (Sequence number=2)\n// bejTupleF\n0x40 //BEJ Enum\n// bejTupleL\n0x01\n0x02 // Length=2\n// bejTupleV\n0x01\n0x01 // Enum value = 1\n```\nI really don't know what it is. But since this BEJ Enum is outside of the main BEJ Set, libbej decode function fails.\n\nAnd in this case as a BMC user I would still want to correctly display these pages, even if RDE device reports some data beyond the root SFLV value length.\n\nSo I think this patchset brings some good. But maybe other users would want different behaviour, so perharps we need to make it conditional (see comment above)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/bej_decoder_core.c",
                    "line": 756,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Konstantin Aladyshev",
                        "email": "aladyshev22@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Kostr"
                    },
                    "message": "Should we make this behaviour conditional?\n\nCurrently you suggest to ignore data beyond the root SFLV's value length. While this would give positive decode results in most cases, I think sometimes users would want to pass the exact buffer with BEJ data and see if it is malformed, i.e:\n- print warning if BEJ has data beyond the root SFLV's value length,\n- return fail if BEJ has data beyond the root SFLV's value length."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/bej_decoder_core.c",
                    "line": 756,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ryan-CJ-Huang",
                        "email": "ryan_huang@jabil.com",
                        "username": "Ryan-CJ-Huang"
                    },
                    "message": "The \"trailing data beyond root SFLV value length\" issue is exactly the kind of device quirk we ran into on our PLDM RDE side too.\n\nI implement 3 policies for libbej user\n\n1. existing IgnoresTrailingBytes keeps validating the default lenient behavior.\n2. new WarnsOnTrailingBytes enables warn, asserts decode returns 0, output matches the unpadded reference, and stderr contains the warning (gtest's CaptureStderr).\n3. new ErrorsOnTrailingBytes enables error, asserts decode returns bejErrorInvalidSize."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/bej_decoder_core.c",
                    "line": 756,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ryan-CJ-Huang",
                        "email": "ryan_huang@jabil.com",
                        "username": "Ryan-CJ-Huang"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
